WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.480
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit 4:
Transport, Cities, and Urban Solutions.

2
00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:11.520
Welcome to Unit 4: Transport, Cities, and Urban Solutions!

3
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:17.160
In this unit you will explore how cities
grow, how people move through them,

4
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.080
and how communities around the world are finding
creative solutions to make urban life better for everyone.

5
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:30.740
You will read about transport systems, green innovations,
and the challenges that cities face in East Africa and beyond.

6
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:36.840
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.920
By the end of this unit,

8
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:45.100
you will be able to read and understand a passage
about city transport and discuss its ideas in english.

9
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:51.580
you will also use prepositions of time and
place (in, on, at) correctly and confidently.

10
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:58.700
you will also form the passive voice in the past
simple, present simple, and with modal verbs.

11
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.280
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:09.920
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
melancholy, exuberant, elated, vulnerable, wary, famished.

13
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:15.900
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

14
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.580
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

15
00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:27.040
The reading sequence includes Transport, Cities, and
Urban Solutions: source text 1 and Transport, Cities,

16
00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:30.120
and Urban Solutions: source text 2.

17
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:31.640
Read actively.

18
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.620
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.440
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.740
The first language focus is Prepositions of Time and Place.

21
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:54.580
What it means and why it matters Prepositions are small but
powerful words that show relationships between other words

22
00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.240
in a sentence.

23
00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:01.180
The three most important prepositions
of time and place are in, on, and at.

24
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.360
Using them correctly makes your English sound natural.

25
00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:12.020
Getting them wrong is one of the most common mistakes
learners make, so this lesson is worth studying carefully.

26
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:19.020
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

27
00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.060
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Vocabulary Expert Interview.

28
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:29.540
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

29
00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:33.200
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

30
00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.800
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

31
00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.380
You are ready to begin.

32
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:45.020
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

33
00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.800
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

34
00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:54.040
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
